  "profile_long": "The provided research materials do not contain any information regarding a dance tradition known as Pique. While the term 'Piqué' is a common technical term in classical ballet, it is absent from the provided ballet glossaries. The only occurrences of the word 'pique' within the source set are found in historical newspaper archives from La Liberté, where it is used as part of the French term 'pique-nique' (picnic). These sources describe community events, such as the 'pique-nique annuel de l'Union nationale métisse' held in June, which involved social gatherings, games, and outdoor activities. Consequently, it is not possible to construct an encyclopedia entry for a dance tradition under this name using the provided documentation.",
